      "id": 1,
      "text": "Glenwood Springs was originally called \"Defiance\" because early white settlers squatted on Ute reservation land.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glenwood_Springs%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was incorporated on September 4, 1885, after the Barlow post office renamed Glenwood Springs in 1884.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glenwood_Springs%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Strawberry Days Festival, founded in 1898, is Colorado's oldest festival and the oldest continuously held civic celebration west of the Mississippi.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glenwood_Springs%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The city sits at the confluence of the Roaring Fork River and the Colorado River, a natural stop for travelers crossing the state.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glenwood_Springs%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Glenwood Springs was one of Colorado's first towns to receive commercially available electricity, putting it ahead of larger settlements in infrastructure.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
